          "Do not return 200 with `{ \"error\": true }` — clients and monitoring look at the code. Typical: 200 OK, 201 Created, 204 No Content, 400 invalid body, 401 unauthenticated, 403 no permission (authenticated), 404 missing resource, 409 state conflict, 412 failed precondition, 422 understood but semantically invalid, 429 too often, 503 temporarily unavailable. Do not mask a 500 as a 400 to 'avoid scaring people'. 301/308 are a permanent move, 302/307 temporary; in APIs be careful with method changes. An error body does not replace the right code.",
          ["Код несе клас результату, не ховайте помилку в 200", "401 vs 403, 404 vs 409 — різні сенси", "5xx не маскують під 4xx"],
